// Build-A-Player College Basketball: generated by the CBB data build (F:/bap-agents/cbb, ESPN feeds pulled 2026-11-11).
// Do not hand-edit counts; re-run the build (gen-current.mjs, then write-data.mjs).
//
// ── Who is here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Every school of the eleven playable conferences (146): its 2026-27 rotation, five guards/wings and four bigs where
// the roster has them (730 guards, 582 bigs). Guards = PG, SG and SF; bigs = PF and C (the game's two basketball
// positions). ESPN lists G, F and C: a forward is a big from 6-8 up, a wing to 6-6, and at 6-7 by what he does (boards
// and blocks against threes and assists). position: PG / SG / SF / PF / C, read the same way.
// The rotation: minutes in the 2026-27 games played so far (ESPN box scores through 2026-11-11), with last season's
// minutes and a freshman's recruiting grade for who hasn't played yet. starter: the five who have started this season
// (at least two guards and a big). depth: 1, 2, 3 ... inside the school's guards, and inside its bigs.
// Bio (number, height, weight, class, photo): ESPN. espn = the ESPN athlete id. year: ESPN's class (FR/SO/JR/SR).
// s27 / s26: his 2026-27 line to date and his 2025-26 line (from: the school he played that season for, a transfer's old one).
// recruit: ESPN's 2026 class rank and grade (freshmen).
//
// ── Grade scale (the NBA pools' 0-11 scale, read against college players) ─────────────────────────────────────
//   0 F · 1 D · 2 C- · 3 C · 4 C+ · 5 B- · 6 B · 7 B+ · 8 A- · 9 A · 10 A+ · 11 S
//   Graded within college, two grades over the same player on the NBA scale (cbbShared collegeGap; Size is the same at
//   both levels). Overall: the game's basketball formula with the college curve (utils/cfbOvr.js collegeOVR).
//   Guards: starters median 81, middle half 78-83, top 95; everyone median 80, middle half 77-83, top 95.
//   Bigs:   starters median 81, middle half 79-85, top 95; everyone median 80, middle half 78-83, top 95.
//
// ── How a grade is made (gen-current.mjs) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. His line: 2025-26 (weight 1 a minute), 2026-27 to date (1.3) and 2024-25 (0.35), per 40 minutes, from ESPN's stats.
// 2. Level: counting stats are scaled by the BPI of the team he played that season for (0.62 to 1.12), so 20 a game
//    in a one-bid league isn't 20 a game in the SEC; a junior college season is far down. November's games count 7% less.
// 3. Percentages are pulled toward an ordinary player's when the attempts are few (60 threes, 40 free throws, 60 twos).
// 4. Quality: his level-adjusted game score per 40, his minutes and his team, on one scale; a freshman's is mostly his
//    ESPN recruiting grade until his minutes come in (420 minutes of prior; 160 for an unranked newcomer).
// 5. A trait = its own numbers (below, as z-scores among rotation players at the position) mixed with his quality
//    (jump shot, passing, rebounding, playmaking mostly their own numbers; IQ, clutch, speed lean on the player he is).
//      Guard  jumpShot 3P% (regressed), FT%, threes made · finishing 2P%, free throws drawn, twos made · passing assists, assist/turnover
//             handles assists, usage, turnover rate, height · perimeterDefense steals, blocks, team defense (BPI), minutes
//             speed height and weight, steals, free throws drawn · bounce blocks, offensive boards, 2P%
//             basketballIQ assist/turnover, eFG%, fouls, class · clutch FT%, scoring, class, minutes
//      Big    jumpShot FT%, threes · finishing 2P%, scoring, free throws drawn · rebounding both boards · playmaking assists, assist/turnover
//             interiorDefense blocks, defensive boards, team defense, height, fouls · speed height and weight, steals · bounce blocks, offensive boards, 2P%
//    Size: from height and weight, the fit of the NBA pools' own Size grades (ovr.mjs sizeOf).
// 6. grade = round(5.95 + 1.5 x z) for guards, round(5.8 + 1.42 x z) for bigs, 1 to 11.
// Not hand-checked against scouting reports yet (College Football's were): these are the numbers' grades.
